              "id": "P32309"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Photoreceptor required for image-forming vision at low light intensity. While most salt water fish species use retinal as chromophore, most freshwater fish use 3-dehydroretinal, or a mixture of retinal and 3-dehydroretinal (By similarity). Light-induced isomerization of 11-cis to all-trans retinal triggers a conformational change that activates signaling via G proteins. Subsequent receptor phosphorylation mediates displacement of the bound G protein alpha subunit by arrestin and terminates signaling (By similarity)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
      "note": {
